---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Squiggle from "../components/Squiggle.astro";
import WaveEdge from "../components/WaveEdge.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What Mile High Family is — and is not.">
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-bg2">
    <div class="blob -left-12 top-0 size-44 bg-sun/30"></div>
    <div class="blob blob-2 right-0 top-10 size-52 bg-navy/10"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow -rotate-1">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 -rotate-1 font-display text-5xl font-extrabold leading-[1.05] text-ink">
        A Colorado site, not a clinic.
      </h1>
      <Squiggle class="mt-3 text-sun" />
    </div>
    <WaveEdge fill="var(--bg)" variant="c" />
  </section>
  <section class="bg-bg">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
      <div class="prose-family squash bg-surface p-8 text-lg leading-relaxed shadow-sm md:p-10">
        <p>
          Mile High Family is a public Front Range site about camping, rockhounding, gymnastics, aviation, and gaming — plus adventures, easy days out, and short lessons. It is written for anyone planning those days, not for a single age band or a “younger family” beat.
        </p>
        <p>
          The bar is straightforward: useful, family-friendly when a mixed group is coming, and honest about effort. If a place needs a reservation, a helmet, or an early start, we say so.
        </p>
        <h2>What you will find</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Camping, rockhounding, gymnastics, aviation, and gaming as first-class sections</li>
          <li>Front Range trips with effort notes and a packing list</li>
          <li>Weekend ideas that still feel like leaving the house</li>
          <li>Lessons you can use the same afternoon</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>What this is not</h2>
        <p>
          This is not a medical practice, a therapy office, or a dentist. Those already use similar names in Denver. We are a lifestyle site about Colorado days.
        </p>
        <p>
          Launch stories are starter editorial for real Colorado places. Photos come from Wikimedia Commons — free, and of the actual spots we name.
        </p>
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          We do not publish children’s full names, school details, or home addresses. If you send a story, we will keep it that way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
